    <summary>Device agent of the OpenFrame platform: installs as a Windows service and connects the machine to your OpenFrame tenant</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[**OpenFrame Client** is the device agent of the [OpenFrame](https://openframe.ai/) platform (remote monitoring and management for MSPs) by Flamingo AI, Inc. It requires an OpenFrame tenant.

Installing the package is step 1 of 2:

1. `choco install openframe-client -y` downloads the signed agent for this package version from openframe.ai, verifies its SHA-256, copies it to `C:\Program Files\OpenFrame\bin\`, adds that folder to the system PATH and registers the Windows service `com.openframe.client`. The service starts and waits; nothing is sent anywhere yet.
2. In a new elevated terminal, run the command shown in your OpenFrame dashboard under **Devices → Add device**:

   `openframe-client auth --serverUrl <tenant host> --initialKey <key> --orgId <organization id> --userId <user id>`

   This connects the device to your tenant. `openframe-client doctor` checks the result.

**Updates are delivered by the OpenFrame platform.** Upgrading this package never changes an installed agent, and installing it again on a machine that already runs the service does nothing.

**Uninstall** (`choco uninstall openframe-client` or `openframe-client uninstall`) stops and removes the service, removes the device from your tenant, uninstalls the integrated tools and deletes the program and data directories.

Documentation: https://github.com/flamingo-stack/openframe-oss-lib/blob/main/clients/README.md#openframe-client-device-agent-install-enrol-remove
]]></description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
